{"id": "wwdc2019-208", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/208", "wordCount": 4174, "segments": [{"start": 16.0, "text": "Hi everyone. My name is Neil Desai [assumed"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "spelling] and I'm a watchOS"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "frameworks engineer and I am"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "really excited to talk to you"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "all about how to create some"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "great independent watch apps."}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "We're increasingly seeing people"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "enjoy being able to go out with"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "just their Apple Watch."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "Users love the quick"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "interactions and the freedom"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "Apple Watch gives them."}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "Whether it's going out with just"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "their watch while working out,"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "running an errand, or quickly"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "answering a call, Apple Watch"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "helps keep you connected to the"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "people, information, and apps"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "you care about most."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "And in these moments where the"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "user is enjoying the freedom of"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "Apple Watch, users think of"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "their iPhone as optional."}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "And we want our watch apps to"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "match our user's expectations of"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "Apple Watch."}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "And to do so we're introducing a"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "new concept, a concept we call"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "independent watch apps."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "So now your iPhone app can be an"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "optional experience."}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "And a lot of apps already are"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "independent to some degree."}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "Outcast is a great example of a"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "podcast app where I can control"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "the entire experience directly"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "from my wrist."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "And CARROT Weather is another"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "great example of an app that I"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "always check the weather on and"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "I only do it on my Apple Watch."}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "And whenever I'm traveling"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "abroad I always use Elk for"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "currency conversions."}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "However, these apps all have an"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "iPhone app."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "And now we're saying that the"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "iPhone app is optional."}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "And for the first time, you can"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "ship a watch only app without"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "having to ship an iOS app at"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "all."}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "Thank you."}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "And to help your apps become"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "independent we're introducing a"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "bunch of new features this year"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "for watch apps, like being able"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "to send push notifications"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "directly to the device, and"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "helping to make sign on even"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "easier and a whole bunch of"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "other features."}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "But first I want to talk about"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "how we actually install these"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "Now up through the Watch iOS 5,"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "the Watch App has been embedded"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "within the iOS app and we"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "download both of them to the"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "iPhone, and then the iPhone"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "handles the task of installing"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "the Watch App from iPhone to"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "Apple Watch."}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "And we're just going to"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "completely change this in iOS 13"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "and watchOS 6."}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "So now the App Store server is"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "going to install whatever it"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "needs to install wherever it"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "needs to install it."}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "And it's going to apply to all"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "applications in the store today."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "And so this means that the iOS"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "app no longer includes that"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "Watch App and some of you may be"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "happy to hear this, the Watch"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "App is no longer going to count"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "against your iOS app cellular"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "download limit."}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "And--  Thank you."}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "And we're able to do this by"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "bitcode recompiling all the apps"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "on our App Store servers and"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "separating out the iOS app from"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "the Watch App."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "And this means that each device"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "is going to download its own"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "So the iPhone gets an iPhone"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "The watch gets a Watch App."}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "And because of this, because"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "we're able to install directly"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "to the device, we're now"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "enabling asset and variant"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "thinning for watch apps for the"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "first time."}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "So if your user has a Series 4"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "device, and, then we can install"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "the appropriate variant and"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "architecture size specific to"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "that device and not any other."}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "And we can apply that same logic"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "to assets."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "So if you've configured your"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "asset catalog to have a"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "particular asset to a particular"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "device, then we can install just"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "that asset to that device."}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "And really this is just a fancy"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "way of saying downloads are much"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "smaller and Watch App binary"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "sizes are much smaller."}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "And if you're using Swift,"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "because of Swift 5 and ABI"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "stability, now the Swift dylibs"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "aren't included within your app"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "at all and so the downloads are"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "going to be even more smaller."}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "And so that's how we install our"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "And let's talk about how our"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "users are going to get them."}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "So your apps are still"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "discoverable in the iOS App"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "Store, but now new in watchOS 6"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "we're introducing the App Store"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "for Apple Watch."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "And it is a fully featured App"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "Store complete with feature"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "sections, full product detail"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "pages, search, editorial."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "And I got to say, you can even"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "purchase an app from your wrist"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "and when it happens it is so"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "cool."}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "I seriously love it."}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "And, so now let's talk about the"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "different types of apps and how"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "they function with this, in this"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "new Watch App Store."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "So all the apps that exist in"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "the store today are what we call"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "dependent apps because the Watch"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "App is considered dependent on"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "the iPhone app by the system."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "And so if I get one of these"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "dependent apps from the Watch"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "App Store on my watch, then the"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "system will kick off a download"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "of the iPhone app to iPhone."}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "And until that happens that the"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "iPhone app is installed, the"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "watchOS app launch is going to"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "be blocked because the system"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "considers that Watch App to be"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "dependent on the iPhone app."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "And now unlike dependent apps,"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "independent apps are where the"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "Watch App can fly solo which"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "means the phone app doesn't need"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "to be installed to launch the"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "Watch App."}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "So that means the Watch App is"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "installed independently."}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "And if your user has both an"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "iPhone and Watch App installed"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "at the same time, now your user"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "can actually uninstall the"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "iPhone app and the Watch App"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "will remain."}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "And for those of you that are a"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "little nervous about, and your"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "brain's already thinking how"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "does this affect my app that"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "exists in the store, you'll be"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "happy to hear that independent"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "watchOS apps with an iOS app are"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "completely backwards compatible"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "with older OS's."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "And those new watch only"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "applications--  Thank you."}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "Thank you. Those new watch only"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "applications are supported on"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "watchOS 6 or later."}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "And if you need to distribute"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "your app within an enterprise"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "for instance, you'll be happy to"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "hear we have full Xcode support"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "to also create those different"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "variants we were talking about"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "to split out your iPhone and"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "Watch App."}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "And new when you go through the"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "flow with Xcode, in the manifest"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "plist that gets generated,"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "there's a new platform"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "identifier key that's added to"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "tell the system what to install"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "and where to install it."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "So now that we know the"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "importance of independent Watch"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "App, let's talk about how to"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "make your watch apps"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "independent."}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "And so let's, by doing so let's"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "jump into Xcode and now I'm"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "going to show you how easy it is"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "to take your existing app and"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "make it independent."}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "Cool. So here we are in Xcode"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "and I have a great Watch App"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "here that's currently a"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "dependent app."}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "And this is-- I've already done"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "all the work to make this app"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "independent, and because it's a"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "great flashcard app that exists"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "on Watch."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "So we can build and run this"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "application and see that the"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "phone simulator and the watch"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "simulator are exactly like we"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "expect in our normal debugging"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "flow."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "And so now the Watch App gets"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "launched and I can immediately"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "start a debugging session."}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "But now let's tell the system to"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "make this app independent."}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "So let's stop that debug session"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "and now in the target editor for"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "our WatchKit extension I see"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "under deployment target there's"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "a new checkbox called supports"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "running without iOS app"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "installation. So I'm going to check that off,"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "and then I'm just going to build"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "and run. And by doing so, by checking off"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "that box, I now told the system"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "it's independent."}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "And I was kind of fast so let me"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "actually show you one cool"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "thing."}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "So let's actually close out the"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "iPhone simulator because this"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "app's independent."}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "Why do we need that iPhone SIM"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "anymore?"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "Let's just build and run once"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "more and now I build and run"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "only to the watch simulator and"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "it provides a much faster"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "debugging experience."}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "Cool. Great."}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "So now let's start and build a"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "watch only application for the"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "first time."}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "So I'm going to close out of"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "this project, and to create a"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "new application I'm just going"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "to go to file, new project, and"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "then under watchOS I see there's"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "a Watch App and then there's"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "also an iOS app with a Watch"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "App."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "And I of course only want to"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "build a watch only app right"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "now."}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "So let's select that."}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "Great."}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "And then of course let's use"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "SwiftUI."}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "It's pretty cool."}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "I hear a lot of good things."}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "And then let's also"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "include a complication."}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "And then let's save that off to"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "my desktop."}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "Perfect. Let's just"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "and now let's just build and"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "run."}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "And again, just like the"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "independent app we were just"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "talking about, we don't need the"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "iPhone simulator, we're just"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "building and running a simple"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "watch only application directly"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "to the watch simulator."}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "Great."}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "Thank you."}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "So we were able to talk about"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "how to migrate your existing app"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "and make it an independent watch"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "We were also able to build a"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "watch only application and we"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "talked about how the simulator"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "experience is much improved."}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "And along the same vein as that"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "simulator experience, let's talk"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "about debugging."}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "So debugging on watchOS 6 is--"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "for simulator is up to 10 times"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "faster now."}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "Thank you."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "And device debugging is up to"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "twice as fast and we've done a"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "lot of work this year to make"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "sure it's more reliable than"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "ever before."}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "And the debugging experience is"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "proxied through iPhone but I"}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "wanted to call out one little"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "pro tip."}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "So if your devices are on Wifi--"}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "your phone and watch-- then a"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "faster route will be chosen by"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "the system and you'll see a much"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "faster debugging experience."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "So let's dive into the different"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "aspects now of how to make an"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "app independent."}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "So to do so we're going to talk"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "about three major things."}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "We're going to talk about how do"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "we get our user data, via"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "authentication or any private"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "user data, directly from our"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "user."}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "We're going to talk about how to push information to the device."}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "And lastly, we're going to talk"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "about dealing with connectivity"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "and gathering our own"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "application data."}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "So let's first talk about"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "authentication."}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "So the primary way to deal with"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "authentication is via sign in"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "and sign up."}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "And now on watchOS 6 you can"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "build sign up auth directly on"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "the watch."}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "And you can support terms and"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "conditions using the WK alert"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "action API."}, {"start": 720.0, "text": "And new on watchOS 6 as well as"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "all of our other Apple"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "platforms, will now support Sign"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "in With Apple."}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "And we're going to talk a little"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "bit about how you can build your"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "own custom password based sign"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "in."}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "So let's first talk about Sign"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "in With Apple."}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "Sign in With Apple is a simple,"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "secure, and private way to get"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "authentication from your user."}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "And your user doesn't have to"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "fill out any forms."}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "There's no new password they"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "have to think of."}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "And they can just simply select"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "an email address and it just"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "continues signing in."}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "And each account has two factor"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "auth built in and there's no"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "email verification that a user"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "has to do."}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "And we support sign in across"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "all devices."}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "And there's also a JavaScript"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "SDK for any other type of"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "device."}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "So to use Sign in With Apple,"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "make sure and use the"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "authentication services"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "framework which is now available"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "on watchOS."}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "And if you have any specific UI"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "you want to build, you can now"}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "use an authorization Apple ID"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "button and embed that within"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "your application."}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "And then once the user actually"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "taps on that button you'll"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "receive your ID action and then"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "you can use the authentication"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "services framework to display"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "the appropriate system UI."}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "And there's a lot of great talks"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "this week."}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "If you want to know some more"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "about Sign in With Apple, I"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "highly recommend them."}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "Great. And to enable Sign in"}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "With Apple in your Xcode project"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "on your WatchKit extension, just"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "add a new capability and enable"}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "your Sign in With Apple"}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "entitlement."}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "And that's how to easily get"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "started."}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "And now you may have your own"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "custom password based sign in"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "and we're introducing a text"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "field new to watchOS this year."}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "And so you can embed this text"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "field from within SwiftUI or"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "WatchKit."}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "And so you can build a UI such"}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "as this where we're just asking"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "our user, hey we just need a"}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "username and password and we're"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "using the placeholder text to"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "instruct our user what to"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "particularly input."}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "And if you set the appropriate"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "text content type for that"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "particular text field, then the"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "system text input controller"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "that gets brought up will change"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "itself for the appropriate text"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "type."}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "And so for this flow, say the"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "user taps on username and then"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "the system text input controller"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "gets brought up."}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "The user can then elect to enter"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "text via dictation or scribble,"}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "and there's now a new option"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "called continuity keyboard."}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "So if a user taps on this, then"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "the Apple Watch will say, hey"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "finish entering some text on"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "your iOS or iPad OS device and"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "you can see they'll receive a"}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "notification on your iPhone or"}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "iPad if they have the same"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "iCloud account logged into it."}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "And if you've ever used tvOS"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "with text fields, this flow will"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "look very familiar."}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "And once the user taps on it,"}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "they can easily enter in text"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "into their iOS keyboard."}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "And again, the text content type"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "like we talked about earlier is"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "going to inform the auto fill"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "suggestions here."}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "And then the user can elect to"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "select an auto fill suggestion"}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "from either their iCloud"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "keychain or the user's preferred"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "password manager."}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "And now to get your-- you want"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "to make sure to get your"}, {"start": 934.0, "text": "password auto fill suggestions"}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "elevated by the system."}, {"start": 937.0, "text": "And so to do that, make sure to"}, {"start": 939.0, "text": "set the correct text content"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "type and add associated domains"}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "to your WatchKit extension."}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "Now associated domains are a"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "great way to tie your app and"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "website together and in this way"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "it lets the system know that hey"}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "the credential that might exist"}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "in the user's iCloud keychain"}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "can get elevated and displayed"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "at the top of the iOS keyboard."}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "And once the user selects on an"}, {"start": 966.0, "text": "auto fill suggestion, then the"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "system will make its best effort"}, {"start": 970.0, "text": "to auto fill both the username"}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "and password at the same time."}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "And for password based sign in,"}, {"start": 976.0, "text": "sometimes you may need to"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "support one time codes."}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "And so if you set the correct"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "text content type, then a"}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "one-time code can get auto"}, {"start": 985.0, "text": "filled if you sent it via maybe"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "an iMessage or a text message,"}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "and then the system text input"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "controller will show that auto"}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "fill suggestion."}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "The user can easily select it"}, {"start": 995.0, "text": "and then go about and continue"}, {"start": 997.0, "text": "with authentication."}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "So again,  text"}, {"start": 1006.0, "text": "field, you can use that from"}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "within SwiftUI or WatchKit."}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "Make sure to set up your"}, {"start": 1012.0, "text": "associated domains to elevate"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "the appropriate auto fill"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "suggestion and test out your"}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "flows with continuity keyboard"}, {"start": 1019.0, "text": "and build one time code support"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "if you need it."}, {"start": 1023.0, "text": "Now, another type of user"}, {"start": 1026.0, "text": "information we sometimes need is"}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "private user information and we"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "want to ask our users for that"}, {"start": 1032.0, "text": "information via the different"}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "frameworks available."}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "Now on watchOS, we've already"}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "supported giving access for"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "calendar, contacts, motion, and"}, {"start": 1041.0, "text": "even other types such as"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "location directly on Apple"}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "Watch. And now with watchOS 6, we now"}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "support giving health"}, {"start": 1049.0, "text": "authorization directly on Apple"}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "Watch."}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "Thank you."}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "So the user can elect to give"}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "access to all of the data"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "requested or even just"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "particular types."}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "So that's how we deal with"}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "getting user data in an"}, {"start": 1069.0, "text": "independent app world."}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "Let's now talk about how to push"}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "information to a device."}, {"start": 1074.0, "text": "And of course the best way to"}, {"start": 1076.0, "text": "push information to a device is"}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "via push notifications."}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "And now with watchOS 6 the watch"}, {"start": 1083.0, "text": "has become a standalone push"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "target for the first time."}, {"start": 1090.0, "text": "And so this means you can send"}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "user visible notifications and"}, {"start": 1095.0, "text": "background notifications"}, {"start": 1096.0, "text": "directly to Apple Watch."}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "And this is based around the"}, {"start": 1100.0, "text": "user notifications framework and"}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "we're using the exact same"}, {"start": 1103.0, "text": "infrastructure as all other"}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "Apple devices."}, {"start": 1107.0, "text": "So from an overview perspective,"}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "your server will send an APNS"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "request header and payload"}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "directly to APNS and APNS is our"}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "Apple Push Notification Service."}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "And then APNS is going to send"}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "that payload down to the"}, {"start": 1121.0, "text": "appropriate device."}, {"start": 1123.0, "text": "On watchOS, the payloads are the"}, {"start": 1125.0, "text": "same as on all other platforms"}, {"start": 1127.0, "text": "we have. And on the APNS request header,"}, {"start": 1130.0, "text": "there's one new key and that new"}, {"start": 1133.0, "text": "key is an APNS push type."}, {"start": 1135.0, "text": "And this is supported on all of"}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "our Apple platforms and on all"}, {"start": 1142.0, "text": "OS's. And so you can set that key to"}, {"start": 1144.0, "text": "be either alert or background."}, {"start": 1147.0, "text": "And the way I like to think"}, {"start": 1148.0, "text": "about this is if the user's ever"}, {"start": 1150.0, "text": "going to see a notification,"}, {"start": 1152.0, "text": "they're going to get alerted to"}, {"start": 1153.0, "text": "something, then set alert in the"}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "push type. And if you need to send a"}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "background notification to just"}, {"start": 1158.0, "text": "wake up your app in the"}, {"start": 1159.0, "text": "background on the user's device"}, {"start": 1162.0, "text": "whenever there's new content"}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "available, you can use the"}, {"start": 1164.0, "text": "background push type."}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "And so for registration and"}, {"start": 1170.0, "text": "delivery for-- for registration"}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "we're going to get our tokens"}, {"start": 1174.0, "text": "for WatchKit."}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "And then just like forwarded"}, {"start": 1177.0, "text": "notifications in past releases,"}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "your alert notifications will"}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "get delivered to your watch apps"}, {"start": 1182.0, "text": "in the same manner as before"}, {"start": 1184.0, "text": "using user notifications in"}, {"start": 1185.0, "text": "conjunction with WatchKit."}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "And your background"}, {"start": 1188.0, "text": "notifications will now get"}, {"start": 1190.0, "text": "delivered on your WK extension"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "delegate."}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "And if you encrypt any of your"}, {"start": 1194.0, "text": "payloads, we now have full"}, {"start": 1196.0, "text": "notification service extension"}, {"start": 1198.0, "text": "support on watchOS as well."}, {"start": 1200.0, "text": "And so you can just decrypt that"}, {"start": 1202.0, "text": "payload directly on the device,"}, {"start": 1203.0, "text": "and then show it to your user."}, {"start": 1207.0, "text": "And in your Xcode project, to"}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "enable push notifications in the"}, {"start": 1211.0, "text": "target editor, if you select"}, {"start": 1212.0, "text": "your WatchKit extension you can"}, {"start": 1214.0, "text": "then just add a new capability"}, {"start": 1216.0, "text": "and enable the push"}, {"start": 1217.0, "text": "notifications entitlement."}, {"start": 1220.0, "text": "And if you want to support"}, {"start": 1221.0, "text": "background notifications, you"}, {"start": 1223.0, "text": "can enable background modes and"}, {"start": 1225.0, "text": "then just enable the remote"}, {"start": 1227.0, "text": "notification checkbox."}, {"start": 1229.0, "text": "So let's dive into some code"}, {"start": 1233.0, "text": "now. So here we are in our extension"}, {"start": 1235.0, "text": "delegate and the application did"}, {"start": 1237.0, "text": "finish launching."}, {"start": 1238.0, "text": "And the first thing we want to"}, {"start": 1239.0, "text": "do when we register for"}, {"start": 1240.0, "text": "notifications is first ask our"}, {"start": 1242.0, "text": "user if that's okay."}, {"start": 1243.0, "text": "So we're going to request"}, {"start": 1245.0, "text": "authorization on our UN user"}, {"start": 1246.0, "text": "notification center."}, {"start": 1247.0, "text": "And if the user elects to grant"}, {"start": 1250.0, "text": "us access, then we can just call"}, {"start": 1252.0, "text": "register for remote"}, {"start": 1253.0, "text": "notifications on our WK shared"}, {"start": 1255.0, "text": "extension."}, {"start": 1256.0, "text": "And after using so, if we"}, {"start": 1260.0, "text": "implement our did register for"}, {"start": 1261.0, "text": "remote notifications call, then"}, {"start": 1264.0, "text": "we can get our device token and"}, {"start": 1266.0, "text": "forward that notification over"}, {"start": 1268.0, "text": "to our notification provider for"}, {"start": 1270.0, "text": "our own server."}, {"start": 1271.0, "text": "And of course we want to make"}, {"start": 1273.0, "text": "sure an implement did fail to"}, {"start": 1275.0, "text": "register to remote notifications"}, {"start": 1277.0, "text": "just in case something failed."}, {"start": 1281.0, "text": "And then for background"}, {"start": 1283.0, "text": "notifications, those will get"}, {"start": 1284.0, "text": "delivered on did receive remote"}, {"start": 1286.0, "text": "notification with a fetch"}, {"start": 1288.0, "text": "completion handler and a"}, {"start": 1289.0, "text": "background fetch result."}, {"start": 1290.0, "text": "So once you receive this you can"}, {"start": 1292.0, "text": "handle your background"}, {"start": 1293.0, "text": "notification and then just call"}, {"start": 1295.0, "text": "the completion handler with"}, {"start": 1296.0, "text": "whatever the appropriate"}, {"start": 1297.0, "text": "background fetch result is."}, {"start": 1302.0, "text": "So again, that APNS push type,"}, {"start": 1304.0, "text": "that new key on the APNS request"}, {"start": 1306.0, "text": "header, is required when sending"}, {"start": 1308.0, "text": "pushes to watchOS."}, {"start": 1310.0, "text": "And it's supported on all"}, {"start": 1311.0, "text": "platforms."}, {"start": 1312.0, "text": "So really if you're sending any"}, {"start": 1314.0, "text": "notifications to any Apple"}, {"start": 1315.0, "text": "devices, just make sure to add"}, {"start": 1317.0, "text": "the APNS push type."}, {"start": 1320.0, "text": "And your APNS topic key on your"}, {"start": 1322.0, "text": "APNS request header is going to"}, {"start": 1324.0, "text": "be your WatchKit apps bundle"}, {"start": 1326.0, "text": "identifier not your WatchKit"}, {"start": 1328.0, "text": "extension. I just want to quickly mention"}, {"start": 1330.0, "text": "that."}, {"start": 1331.0, "text": "And if you have multiple apps"}, {"start": 1333.0, "text": "like an iPhone app and a Watch"}, {"start": 1335.0, "text": "App, you want to send your"}, {"start": 1336.0, "text": "notifications to both devices"}, {"start": 1338.0, "text": "simultaneously."}, {"start": 1339.0, "text": "And when you do so, the system"}, {"start": 1342.0, "text": "will appropriately de-duplicate"}, {"start": 1344.0, "text": "the notifications when they're"}, {"start": 1345.0, "text": "sent simultaneously."}, {"start": 1349.0, "text": "And another great way to push"}, {"start": 1351.0, "text": "information to a device is via"}, {"start": 1352.0, "text": "complication pushes."}, {"start": 1355.0, "text": "So complication pushes are a"}, {"start": 1356.0, "text": "great way to update your app if"}, {"start": 1359.0, "text": "your complication is enabled on"}, {"start": 1361.0, "text": "the active watch face."}, {"start": 1365.0, "text": "And this is done via PushKit"}, {"start": 1367.0, "text": "which has now been made available on watchOS."}, {"start": 1369.0, "text": "And you can use PushKit for both"}, {"start": 1371.0, "text": "your registration and delivery."}, {"start": 1374.0, "text": "So if you're using the old"}, {"start": 1375.0, "text": "complication push mechanism"}, {"start": 1377.0, "text": "that's based on iOS, we"}, {"start": 1379.0, "text": "recommend you just send your"}, {"start": 1380.0, "text": "complication pushes directly to"}, {"start": 1382.0, "text": "the watch now."}, {"start": 1385.0, "text": "So in code, we can just register"}, {"start": 1388.0, "text": "for complication pushes by"}, {"start": 1389.0, "text": "setting up our PK push registry,"}, {"start": 1392.0, "text": "set up our delegate, and then"}, {"start": 1394.0, "text": "specify some desired push types."}, {"start": 1399.0, "text": "And then once we do so we're"}, {"start": 1400.0, "text": "going to get our device token"}, {"start": 1402.0, "text": "and we just forward that off to"}, {"start": 1404.0, "text": "our server and handle any"}, {"start": 1406.0, "text": "invalidations that might occur."}, {"start": 1409.0, "text": "And then when we actually send a"}, {"start": 1410.0, "text": "push and deliver one, then we"}, {"start": 1413.0, "text": "just implement the appropriate"}, {"start": 1415.0, "text": "PushKit method and just handle"}, {"start": 1417.0, "text": "receiving that complication push"}, {"start": 1419.0, "text": "and then reload our complication"}, {"start": 1421.0, "text": "timeline."}, {"start": 1424.0, "text": "So great."}, {"start": 1425.0, "text": "That's how we push information"}, {"start": 1426.0, "text": "to a device."}, {"start": 1428.0, "text": "Now let's talk about how to"}, {"start": 1429.0, "text": "gather application data and deal"}, {"start": 1432.0, "text": "with connectivity."}, {"start": 1434.0, "text": "So in general in terms of"}, {"start": 1436.0, "text": "networking, we want to use"}, {"start": 1438.0, "text": "URLSession which has been"}, {"start": 1440.0, "text": "available for quite some time on"}, {"start": 1441.0, "text": "watchOS."}, {"start": 1442.0, "text": "And for those that use CloudKit,"}, {"start": 1446.0, "text": "we can also use CloudKit to"}, {"start": 1447.0, "text": "gather application data."}, {"start": 1451.0, "text": "So if you're using watch"}, {"start": 1453.0, "text": "connectivity and depending on"}, {"start": 1454.0, "text": "your iPhone app for any"}, {"start": 1456.0, "text": "particular data, you're going to"}, {"start": 1457.0, "text": "want to migrate all of your"}, {"start": 1459.0, "text": "watch connectivity usage over to"}, {"start": 1461.0, "text": "NSURLSession."}, {"start": 1462.0, "text": "And again, the watch, a lot of"}, {"start": 1466.0, "text": "times users will only use their"}, {"start": 1468.0, "text": "Watch App for a couple seconds"}, {"start": 1469.0, "text": "and then immediately put their"}, {"start": 1470.0, "text": "wrist down, so make sure to use"}, {"start": 1473.0, "text": "background sessions to ensure"}, {"start": 1474.0, "text": "that your URLSessions will"}, {"start": 1476.0, "text": "appropriately complete."}, {"start": 1480.0, "text": "And so watch connectivity is"}, {"start": 1482.0, "text": "still available and you can"}, {"start": 1484.0, "text": "still use for any companion"}, {"start": 1486.0, "text": "app's specific interactions."}, {"start": 1488.0, "text": "But really only use it if you"}, {"start": 1490.0, "text": "really need to."}, {"start": 1491.0, "text": "And there's a Boolean property"}, {"start": 1494.0, "text": "is companion app installed to"}, {"start": 1496.0, "text": "let you know whether or not the"}, {"start": 1497.0, "text": "iPhone app is there."}, {"start": 1502.0, "text": "So in CloudKit, if you're"}, {"start": 1505.0, "text": "already using it you'll be happy"}, {"start": 1506.0, "text": "to hear we have full CK"}, {"start": 1508.0, "text": "subscription support now on"}, {"start": 1510.0, "text": "watchOS and, which goes hand in"}, {"start": 1513.0, "text": "hand with supporting CloudKit"}, {"start": 1514.0, "text": "notifications."}, {"start": 1515.0, "text": "So if you don't want to manage"}, {"start": 1516.0, "text": "your own server or notification"}, {"start": 1518.0, "text": "provider, you can just use"}, {"start": 1520.0, "text": "CloudKit to send notifications."}, {"start": 1522.0, "text": "And there's a great talk"}, {"start": 1524.0, "text": "available online if you want to"}, {"start": 1526.0, "text": "check out some more information"}, {"start": 1527.0, "text": "about CloudKit and its best"}, {"start": 1529.0, "text": "practices."}, {"start": 1531.0, "text": "And so for CK subscriptions,"}, {"start": 1533.0, "text": "they're a great way to subscribe"}, {"start": 1535.0, "text": "to database changes that are"}, {"start": 1537.0, "text": "occurring on any other devices."}, {"start": 1539.0, "text": "And then you'll get a background"}, {"start": 1541.0, "text": "push notification that'll tell"}, {"start": 1543.0, "text": "you when to update your"}, {"start": 1544.0, "text": "application and then you can"}, {"start": 1546.0, "text": "retrieve only what has changed"}, {"start": 1548.0, "text": "between your app and your"}, {"start": 1549.0, "text": "CloudKit container."}, {"start": 1552.0, "text": "And from a high level look at"}, {"start": 1554.0, "text": "it, say your user is using an"}, {"start": 1557.0, "text": "iPhone app and they made a"}, {"start": 1558.0, "text": "database change."}, {"start": 1559.0, "text": "That database change will get"}, {"start": 1561.0, "text": "sent to the CloudKit and then"}, {"start": 1563.0, "text": "CloudKit's going to realize, oh"}, {"start": 1565.0, "text": "hey, there's a subscription, and"}, {"start": 1567.0, "text": "then CloudKit will then tell"}, {"start": 1569.0, "text": "APNS to send a background"}, {"start": 1571.0, "text": "notification down to any other"}, {"start": 1573.0, "text": "device that has a subscription,"}, {"start": 1575.0, "text": "in this case, our Watch App."}, {"start": 1579.0, "text": "And then if the Watch App, if"}, {"start": 1581.0, "text": "the user makes a change with the"}, {"start": 1583.0, "text": "Watch App, then the cycle will"}, {"start": 1584.0, "text": "just repeat itself."}, {"start": 1586.0, "text": "And how we send notifications is"}, {"start": 1589.0, "text": "governed by the exact same rules"}, {"start": 1591.0, "text": "as on all of our other devices."}, {"start": 1593.0, "text": "To set up your CloudKit"}, {"start": 1596.0, "text": "subscriptions, you can set up"}, {"start": 1597.0, "text": "your notification info and then"}, {"start": 1599.0, "text": "make sure and set your should"}, {"start": 1601.0, "text": "send content available to be"}, {"start": 1602.0, "text": "true."}, {"start": 1603.0, "text": "And then CloudKit's going to"}, {"start": 1605.0, "text": "deliver your push on that same"}, {"start": 1607.0, "text": "delegate callback we were"}, {"start": 1608.0, "text": "talking about earlier, your did"}, {"start": 1609.0, "text": "receive remote notification."}, {"start": 1611.0, "text": "So then you can just handle that"}, {"start": 1612.0, "text": "and retrieve only what has"}, {"start": 1614.0, "text": "changed between your app and the"}, {"start": 1616.0, "text": "CloudKit container."}, {"start": 1619.0, "text": "So great. Those are the three"}, {"start": 1621.0, "text": "major ways we think about how to"}, {"start": 1623.0, "text": "make watch apps independent."}, {"start": 1625.0, "text": "How do we get user data and then"}, {"start": 1628.0, "text": "also how do we push information"}, {"start": 1630.0, "text": "down to the device?"}, {"start": 1631.0, "text": "And lastly, how do we actually"}, {"start": 1633.0, "text": "deal with getting our own"}, {"start": 1634.0, "text": "application data?"}, {"start": 1639.0, "text": "So users love the freedom and"}, {"start": 1642.0, "text": "independence that Apple Watch"}, {"start": 1643.0, "text": "gives them and now there are a"}, {"start": 1645.0, "text": "bunch of system and developer"}, {"start": 1647.0, "text": "capabilities at your disposal."}, {"start": 1649.0, "text": "So make sure to make your watch"}, {"start": 1650.0, "text": "apps independent because,"}, {"start": 1652.0, "text": "honestly, customers probably"}, {"start": 1654.0, "text": "already expect their watch apps"}, {"start": 1656.0, "text": "to be independent, and now more"}, {"start": 1658.0, "text": "than ever."}, {"start": 1659.0, "text": "So there's some great"}, {"start": 1662.0, "text": "information available online"}, {"start": 1664.0, "text": "with some sessions and labs."}, {"start": 1666.0, "text": "And thank you all everyone for"}, {"start": 1668.0, "text": "coming and I hope you all have a"}, {"start": 1669.0, "text": "great WWDC."}]}